es and a placeholder audio cue. Native Luganda, early-years, cultural, accessibility, and final-media review are still required.","evidenceBoundary":"Completion records exposure or supported selection only; it does not prove speaking, independent recall, or mastery."}}],"metadata":{"reviewStatus":"Draft text plus temporary bundled images and a placeholder audio cue. Native Luganda, early-years, cultural, accessibility, and final-media review are still required.","implementationStatus":"playable-technical-draft"}},{"id":"lg-s2-l6-body-feelings-review","order":6,"title":"Body and feelings review","description":"Choose the best answer in five short review questions.","mechanic":"mini_quiz","isStartable":true,"isLocked":false,"readiness":"placeholder","status":"startable","items":[{"id":"lg-s2-l6-quiz","mechanic":"mini_quiz","order":1,"title":"Body and feelings review","instructions":"Londa eky'okuddamu ekituufu. / Choose the best answer.","questions":[{"id":"lg-s2-q01","promptText":"Londa ekigambo ekitegeeza 'head'. / Choose the Luganda word for head.","promptEnglishText":"Choose the Luganda word for head.","correctOptionId":"lg-body-head","options":[{"id":"lg-body-head","text":"Omutwe","englishText":"Head"},{"id":"lg-body-ears","text":"Amatu","englishText":"Ears"},{"id":"lg-body-foot","text":"Ekigere","englishText":"Foot"}],"explanationText":"Omutwe means \"head.\""},{"id":"lg-s2-q02","promptText":"Londa ekigambo ekitegeeza 'ears'. / Choose the Luganda word for ears.","promptEnglishText":"Choose the Luganda word for ears.","correctOptionId":"lg-body-ears","options":[{"id":"lg-body-eyes","text":"Amaaso","englishText":"Eyes"},{"id":"lg-body-ears","text":"Amatu","englishText":"Ears"},{"id":"lg-body-mouth","text":"Akamwa","englishText":"Mouth"}],"explanationText":"Amatu means \"ears.\""},{"id":"lg-s2-q03","promptText":"Mu Luganda, ogamba otya nti 'I am happy'? / How do you say \"I am happy\" in Luganda?","promptEnglishText":"How do you say \"I am happy\" in Luganda?","cor